  '<p class="gd-p">Marketing writes the text of every ad from the car&#39;s own record, keeps track of where each ad is posted, tells the sales assistants when an ad needs updating, shows which channels bring bookings, drafts the week&#39;s Facebook Page and Instagram posts and keeps the consent log for owner recruitment. Nothing is posted by the server: you post by hand, and Facebook Marketplace from the owner&#39;s own profile, with a kit and a daily rotation under Marketplace.</p><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-facebook-marketplace" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Facebook Marketplace</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Marketplace</b>. Listings go up from the owner&#39;s own Facebook profile (business Pages cannot post vehicles), by Claude in the owner&#39;s Chrome or by a person. The playbook is docs/runbooks/marketplace.md.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Today</b> lists what is due: <b class="gd-ui">Update the price</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Take down</b> first, then up to the day&#39;s allowance of new posts and renewals (4 a day by default: 3 to 5 a day avoids spam flags). <b class="gd-ui">Coming up</b> shows the next days.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Kit</b> on a car. The kit shows every field of facebook.com/marketplace/create/vehicle in the form&#39;s order (location, year, make, model, mileage, price, body style, colours, condition, fuel, transmission), each with <b class="gd-ui">Copy</b>, the description in Marketplace style, and the tracked link.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Download the photos (ZIP)</b>. It has the 10 best photos named 01 to 10. Add them in that order: the first is the cover.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Post it. Then press <b class="gd-ui">Posted</b> on Today and paste the listing&#39;s address. Press <b class="gd-ui">Renewed</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Updated</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Taken down</b> the same way when you do those.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Inbox replies for this car</b> has the answers for price, availability, requirements, deposit, delivery and &quot;send your number&quot;, filled in for the car. Each one ends with the car&#39;s link or asks for a phone number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">After answering the inbox, open <b class="gd-ui">Log an inbox session</b>. Enter the number of chats and the numbers collected, one per line (name, phone, car code). Each new number becomes a lead, and customer service gets a call-back task due within 15 minutes.</div></li></ol></div><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Kits are made when the page opens, so their prices are today&#39;s. A price change marks the live listing <b class="gd-ui">Update the price</b> and opens the usual update task.</li><li>A car that does not take requests, has no daily rate or has only sample photos says <b class="gd-ui">Do not post yet</b>.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Rotation settings</b> change the posts a day, the days before a renewal, and the default location (a car&#39;s home area wins).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">The team&#39;s listings</b>: Sales post from their own profiles under <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b>, each listing in its own copy variant (title, description, photo order and cover), so no ad is posted twice. A car has at most 5 live listings, yours included (<b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Facebook Marketplace</b>). The card lists who posted what, its status, when it ends and the listing&#39;s address. Your own posts and renewals still count against your own day only.</li><li>The booking request asks &quot;How did you hear about us?&quot; (optional). Bookings by channel counts the answer after staff&#39;s source and a tracked visit.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-write-an-ad" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Write an ad</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Ads</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Ad listings</b> tab.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the car and the channel (Facebook Marketplace, Kijiji, Craigslist, Instagram, Facebook Page or Google Business Profile) and press <b class="gd-ui">Write it</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Copy each part with its button: the title, the price line, the description (or caption), the hashtags and the tracked link. Each shows its length against the channel&#39;s limit (a Kijiji title takes 64 characters, Craigslist 70, an Instagram caption 2,200, a Google post 1,500).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Add the photos in the order shown: the first is the cover. Open a photo to save it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Post the ad on the site, then press <b class="gd-ui">Mark as posted</b> and paste its address and the date.</div></li></ol></div><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The text comes from the car&#39;s record only: the rates, kilometres, deposit, delivery fee, who may rent it and the car code. A fact the record does not have is left out. No review, rating or claim is added.</li><li>The tracked link opens the car&#39;s page with utm_source (the channel), utm_medium and utm_campaign (the car code), so the request counts under that channel.</li><li>A warning shows when the car does not take requests, has no daily rate, or shows sample photos (take real photos first: an ad shows the car itself).</li><li>Facebook Marketplace is posted from the owner&#39;s own Facebook profile in their browser: Meta does not take vehicle listings from business Pages. Kijiji takes one ad per car, in one category and one region. An Instagram caption cannot hold a working link: put it in the bio or a story link sticker.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-when-an-ad-needs-updating" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">When an ad needs updating</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Posted ads</b>, or the task in <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff tasks</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A change of 3% or more in a car&#39;s daily, weekend, weekly or 30-day rate, any change of its deposit, kilometres, extra-km price or delivery fee, or the car leaving the site marks each of its live ads Needs updating and opens a task for the sales assistants (for example Update the Kijiji ad and the car). The task says what changed, the new price line and the ad&#39;s address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">New text</b>, copy the new text and update the ad on the site.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Mark the ad updated</b>. The task closes. Closing the task in Staff tasks counts too.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Car off the site: take the ad down and press <b class="gd-ui">Taken down</b>. If the car comes back at the same rates first, the task is cancelled by itself.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The 3% is under <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, Advertising and owner recruitment. The rates are checked again every 6 hours, so a rate dated ahead is caught on its day.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-bookings-by-channel" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Bookings by channel</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Bookings by channel</b>.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Every request of the dates chosen counts once: under the source staff set on the booking, else the renter&#39;s visit (the campaign source of a tracked link, or the site they came from), else a referral code, else how it reached us (phone, email, WhatsApp).</li><li>Choose the last visit before the request or the first visit. A booking is a request that was confirmed, paid or completed; revenue is its rental charge after discounts. The months add up to the Bookings list.</li><li>The visit is kept with the request when it is sent, so the source outlives the 90 days of visit history. A visitor who refused analytics cookies has no source.</li><li>On a booking, the line Came from shows the source. Press <b class="gd-ui">Set</b> to give it by hand when the renter told you (a Kijiji reply, a walk-in, word of mouth).</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-facebook-page-and-instagram-drafts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Facebook Page and Instagram drafts</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Social drafts</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The week&#39;s drafts are written from the fleet every 6 hours, for this week and the next: Monday a new car (published in the last 14 days) or a featured one; Tuesday the owner program; Thursday the cars free this weekend; Friday the requirements (Instagram); Sunday a price highlight or a seasonal trip (Facebook Page). Press <b class="gd-ui">Write drafts for this week</b> to write them now.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Read each draft. Press <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> to change the caption, the channels or the day, then <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>; or press <b class="gd-ui">Skip</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Copy the caption for each channel (on the Facebook Page the tracked link is in the text; for Instagram copy the link for the bio), post it with the photos shown, then press <b class="gd-ui">Posted on Instagram</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Posted on Facebook Page</b> and paste the post&#39;s address.</div></li></ol></div><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Wednesday&#39;s walkaround video and Saturday&#39;s handover story are filmed by field staff. No renter is shown without written consent.</li><li>Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a post of your own</b> at the bottom of the week for anything else.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-meta-publishing-off-until-set-up" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Meta publishing (off until set up)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Meta publishing</b>. Until it is on, every post is copied and posted by hand.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Make the Instagram account a professional account and link it to the CarmaCars Facebook Page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">At developers.facebook.com, create a Business app owned by the CarmaCars business portfolio. Give it the permissions pages_show_list, pages_read_engagement, pages_manage_posts, instagram_basic and instagram_content_publish, and make a long-lived Page access token. Meta may ask for App Review before posts are public.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Enter the details</b>: the Page id, the Instagram account id and the token. The token goes to the vault; the page shows only its last four characters.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Switch on</b>. Approved drafts then go out on their day and their post links are recorded; a refusal shows on the draft. Press <b class="gd-ui">Switch off</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Remove the token</b> at any time.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-scheduled-posts-facebook-instagram-tiktok" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Scheduled posts (Facebook, Instagram, TikTok)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Social drafts</b>, the Scheduled posts card at the top. Sales have the same card on their Marketing page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose where (Facebook Page, Instagram or TikTok) and when. Pick a draft for its caption and link (and its photo), or write the caption. Pick a short video if you made one. Press <b class="gd-ui">Schedule</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Every 5 minutes the database marks the posts whose time has come as due. With Meta publishing switched on, Facebook and Instagram posts go out by themselves (photos, Page videos and Instagram reels) and the post link is recorded; Meta refusing three times makes the post Failed with Meta&#39;s answer and a Try again button.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Without Meta publishing the card says <b class="gd-ui">Connect Meta</b> and works as a queue: at its time a post is due with the caption to copy and the photo or video to download. Post it, then press <b class="gd-ui">Posted by hand</b> and paste the post&#39;s address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">TikTok is always by hand (its posting API needs TikTok&#39;s app review): a due TikTok post shows the checklist. Download the video, post it in the TikTok app with the caption, copy the link, press <b class="gd-ui">Posted by hand</b>.</div></li></ol></div><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Instagram needs a photo or an MP4 video; TikTok needs a video. Every change is in the post&#39;s Log.</li><li>Facebook Marketplace has no posting API: keep using the Marketplace kit and its session flow.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-short-video-for-reels-tiktok-and-stories" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Short video for Reels, TikTok and Stories</h2><p class="gd-p">On a listing (below First photo) or in <b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Marketplace</b>, the car&#39;s kit.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Make a short video</b>. Your browser draws a 9:16 video from the car&#39;s approved photos: a slow zoom on each, the brand at the top, the car, the price a day and the call to action at the bottom. Keep the tab in front until it says Saved (about 20 seconds for 8 photos).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Download</b> to post it yourself, or schedule it in Scheduled posts. <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes it off the list.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The words and timing are <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>: social video call to action ({price} is the live price a day), brand, seconds a photo and photos a video. It is free: nothing is sent to a paid service.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-make-the-missing-angle" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Make the missing angle</h2><p class="gd-p">On a listing (below First photo) or in the Marketplace kit: for a required angle the car has no photo of.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Make Rear</b> (or the angle missing). The image model makes that view from the car&#39;s approved photos, only within its free daily use (the showroom&#39;s limit).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check the view: same car, same colour, wheels and badges, no damage hidden or added. Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Reject</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>An approved view shows on the site after the real photos, labelled AI view. It is never the cover and never used as damage or condition evidence (handovers, claims). Take the real photo when you can: a real photo of the angle replaces the view at once.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-owner-recruitment" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner recruitment</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner recruitment</b>.</p><p class="gd-p">Owners and co-hosts are found in classified ads. The anti-spam law (CASL) does not cover a live phone call, but an email or a text needs consent, names the sender and offers an unsubscribe. The lawyer confirms the approach before outreach starts.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a lead</b>: paste the ad&#39;s address, choose who is selling (a private seller, a dealer or a rental business) and type the name, the phone and the car from the ad. Nothing is collected from the classified site.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Call them with the script on the lead&#39;s page and press <b class="gd-ui">Log the call</b>. A yes needs their words (&quot;Yes, text me the details&quot;): they become express consent in the log. A no means do not contact, ever.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When the lead&#39;s page says email or text is allowed, choose a template, check the words and press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b>. The email adds CarmaCars&#39; name, mailing address and the unsubscribe link; the text ends with &quot;Reply STOP to opt out.&quot; Texts wait for 8 am during quiet hours.</div></li></ol></div><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Press <b class="gd-ui">Record consent</b> for consent given another way: express (with its proof), implied by their inquiry (6 months), implied by a business relationship (2 years), a business address published with no &quot;no solicitation&quot; note (never a private seller), or one message after a referral (naming the referrer).</li><li>The consent log is never edited: a change is a new line. An unsubscribe or a STOP reply adds a withdrawal by itself, and nothing more goes on that channel.</li><li>A message without consent is refused with the reason. <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b> has a switch that stops all recruitment messages.</li></ul><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Keep the proof of an oral yes: a recording, or a note written during the call with the time. Consent you cannot show does not count.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-owner-pipeline" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner pipeline</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner pipeline</b>. Every prospective owner is one card, in one of eight columns: New, Contacted, Call booked, Applied, Agreement sent, Signed, Car onboarded and Lost. Leads come from the owner form on the website, an owner&#39;s referral link, Owner recruitment (classified ads) and <b class="gd-ui">Add an owner lead</b>. A visitor who starts the application is a lead as soon as a valid email or mobile is typed (Website form, unfinished), with the car they entered or priced in the earnings calculator; the same email or phone joins the lead already open.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Follow-up emails go by themselves on day 0, 2, 5 and 10 after a lead comes in: the owner program in plain words (the car goes on our fleet insurance policy, we rent it out in Toronto and pay the owner every month; fees apply) and the link to apply. They are marketing emails: they wait behind every other email under the daily limit, go in the sending hours and carry the unsubscribe link.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">They go only with consent: a website inquiry counts for 6 months, a classified-ad lead needs consent in its log, and a referral typed by staff gets one message only.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">They stop when the lead replies (a text or a call from their number, or press <b class="gd-ui">They replied</b>), when the stage changes, when they unsubscribe, and after the last one. <b class="gd-ui">Stop follow-ups</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Restart follow-ups</b> are on each card.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Move</b> changes the stage (with a note, and why when lost). Agreement sent, Signed and Car onboarded also follow the owner&#39;s records: an owner agreement sent or signed, a car on the site.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Customer service sees the same board in the staff portal. Sales see only the owners they invited, added or were given, on My sales.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A new website lead goes to the least busy Sales person, never to a verification or test account (with no real Sales person on, it waits unassigned). Test accounts are never &quot;sourced by&quot; on a real lead or owner, nor given its task.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">An application left unfinished for 30 minutes goes to the least busy Sales person with a task, and its follow-ups say &quot;finish your application&quot; with a link that opens their saved answers. When they send it, the card moves to Applied and the follow-ups stop.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Leads that came in before the automatic follow-ups existed and that nobody moved are in To do as a task &quot;Follow up now&quot; with their name: call or email them, then move the card.</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Owner referral links</h3><p class="gd-p">An owner&#39;s link for new owners is <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/r/&lt;their code&gt;?to=owner</span> (the list is at the bottom of the board). A new owner who applies after it is credited to that owner. The credit follows the referral kickback rule: the Kickback Rate (20%) of the Rental Charge of the first completed rental of the new owner&#39;s car. It shows under <b class="gd-ui">Owner referral credits</b> as due; pay it with the owner&#39;s payout and press <b class="gd-ui">Mark paid</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-listing-channels" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Listing channels</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listing channels</b>: the sites and directories where our cars can be listed beyond carmacars.ca (Turo, Getaround, Google Business Profile, Google Merchant Center, the Meta catalog, Kijiji, Facebook Marketplace, KAYAK, Expedia, Discover Cars, Rentalcars.com, Craigslist, Bing Places, Apple Business Connect, Yelp, YellowPages and any you add).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each has a status (Not started, Applied, Live, Paused, Not for us), who holds the login, notes and how listing works there. Press <b class="gd-ui">Update</b> to change them, <b class="gd-ui">Add a channel</b> for a new one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">None is connected by itself: apply on the site. When a site or partner program takes a feed, give it that channel&#39;s address: <b class="gd-ui">JSON</b>, <b class="gd-ui">CSV</b> or <b class="gd-ui">XML</b> (the XML is in the shape of Google&#39;s vehicle listings feed). Car links carry the channel, so its bookings show in Bookings by channel.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Every feed has our own and co-hosted cars on the site, never a partner&#39;s car (01 Motors or any other). <b class="gd-ui">Keep out</b> takes a car out of every feed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">New key</b> ends the old address. Each feed is read at most 60 times an hour and each answer is kept 15 minutes.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'fleet', 'chapter', 'finance', 'You keep the cars moving: field jobs, daily checks, photo reviews after returns, and the listings with their duplicate check and plate covering.

Your rail: Queue, Today, Field jobs, Field hours, Daily checks, Photo reviews, Calendar, Listings, Similar cars, Find a renter and Scorecard.

## Schedule field jobs

Every confirmed booking gets its handover (or delivery) and return (or pickup) jobs by itself, at the booking''s times and place, and put on a shift: the shift covering its time, or that day''s (see Shifts and who gets a job). The people on the shift share its jobs, least busy first. You check and change them.

1. Jobs, next three days: each with its place, its shift, its field staff and whether they acknowledged it. "Made from the booking" marks the ones made by themselves; when the booking moves, they move too, unless you changed them.
2. Change a job with **To a shift** (another shift), **Assign** or **Reassign** (a field person on a shift that day when the day has shifts, or an Admin), **Move** (time and place) or **Cancel**.
3. Handovers and returns without a job (when the automatic jobs are off, or one was cancelled) are listed first: press **Schedule**, the place filled in from the booking.
4. An Admin turns the automatic jobs or the assignment off in Settings > Program.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-02-field-jobs-desktop-8e721230.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 565; address: carmacars.ca/va/fleet; pins: 1 17.9 51.3")

## Shifts and who gets a job

Field staff take their shifts from a schedule you publish, ideally a week ahead. A job is given by itself only to a field person who passed the academy and holds a shift that day, and work lands only on days with shifts.

1. On **Field jobs**, **Shifts, next seven days** shows each day and how many people are on a shift, and each shift its jobs (**Jobs on it**). A shift with jobs and nobody on it is marked; within 24 hours of its start you get an alert and a To do, once.
2. Press **Publish shifts**: the first day''s start and end, how many people, and for how many days the same hours repeat. Field staff take them on their phones.
3. **Add a person** puts someone on a shift and **Remove** takes them off. A person who has not passed the academy cannot take shifts or be given a job.
4. A shift nobody claimed keeps its jobs: field staff see them when they look for shifts to claim, and the one who claims it gets them. A shift given up or swapped takes its jobs along; a cancelled shift sends them to another shift.
5. Work due on a day with no shifts moves to the day before when it is known in advance, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day. The job shows its planned day and keeps the booking''s real time; the renter''s times never change. A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning: cover it, or move the booking time.
6. **Unassign** takes a job off its person and its shift; tick **Tell them** only if they should know. The Admins can be given a job too (no shift needed).

## Fleet map

At the top of **Field jobs**: every car on the map with its renter, booking, due-back time and state, the alerts, and the trips by booking, the same as the Admin''s. Only Admins and fleet staff see positions.

1. Press a car for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery and the trip under way.
2. An alert (speeding, left Ontario or the zone, still driving after the return time, low or unplugged tracker, not reporting) also comes to your bell and as an urgent phone alert. Call the renter, then press **Seen**.
3. A car still driving after its return time: call, send the late notice and offer a paid extension, as for any late return.

## Field hours

Field staff clock in and out on their phones. You see who is clocked in and every shift of the two-week pay period, and you fix what they cannot.

1. Open **Field hours**. **Clocked in now** lists who is on, since when. **Earlier period** and **Later period** move between pay periods.
2. Someone forgot to clock out: press **Clock out for them**, set the time they finished and write the reason.
3. Someone forgot to clock in, or a time is wrong: **Add hours** enters a shift, **Change** fixes one and **Remove** takes one out. Each needs a reason; the change is kept in a log with what it was before.
4. Once an Admin approves the pay run of a period, its shifts are locked: ask the Admin. You see hours only, not rates or pay.

### Where they clocked in
The hours list shows where each person clocked in and out: a map link and the distance from the lot. A clock in or out over 500 m away, or with the location refused, is shown in bold with the reason the person wrote. Their location is asked only at those two moments, never in between.

## Daily checks

Twice a day: the opening check by 9:00 and the closing check by 18:00.

1. Open **Daily checks** and choose **Opening check** or **Closing check**.
2. Each line shows what was found. Tick OK, or Problem with a note.
3. Press **Save the opening check** (or **Save the closing check**). You can save it again.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-03-daily-checks-desktop-be06d6c0.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 820; address: carmacars.ca/va/checks; pins: 1 6.5 15.4, 2 44.7 42.0, 3 64.2 94.0")

## Check a car out or in

Fleet, Sales and Customer service check cars out and in from the booking.

1. On a confirmed booking press **Check in (pickup)**; on a booking on rent, **Check out (return)**. Today lists the ones due, each with its button.
2. The checklist field staff use opens: readings (km and fuel or charge), the photo set with the plate and the gauges, damage close-ups and both signatures.
3. Afterwards press **Photo report**: times, Late by, kilometres, fuel, photos and the return charges. Fleet waives a charge with **Waive** and a reason.

## Photo reviews after a return

After each return, the field photo set waits under **Photo reviews**. Compare it with the pickup set. Press **Review done**, or **Ask for a re-shoot** if a photo is missing or unclear.

## Similar cars

A possible duplicate never keeps a car off the site: it shows on the car''s checklist until you decide. Only Same car takes it off.

1. Each flag shows the car, what it looks like (same VIN, plate, photo or specs) and the other car.
2. Compare the permit, the plate and the photos.
3. Press **Not a duplicate** with a note when they are different cars, or **Same car** when they are.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-06-similar-cars-desktop-562b0382.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 460; address: carmacars.ca/va/similar-cars; pins: 1 23.6 30.4, 3 94.8 30.4")

## Rates and kilometres

From a listing, press **The car and its rates**, or open the car from Field jobs and its **Rates & fees** tab.

1. Type the rates an Admin set. Only the daily rate is needed; the others follow from it when empty. The weekend rate is a price per day for each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday.
2. Keep **Use the defaults** for the kilometres, or choose **Custom for this car**.
3. Check What renters pay under the fields, then press **Save the rates**. Rates, kilometres and deposit save together.
4. **Price limits**, below: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts, read only. Offers, promo codes and lead-time pricing stay between them; an Admin or the owner changes them, and only an Admin allows one booking outside them.

## Listings and covering plates

1. Open **Listings**. A draft waiting shows Needs review. Open it.
2. The copy is written by itself (change a line only if you must: it is then kept). Check the photos: on each public photo, cover the plate or mark it not visible.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-05-listings-desktop-d2672e0a.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 340; address: carmacars.ca/va/listings; pins: 1 54.5 49.1")

3. The listing''s Steps to go live says what is next: 1 Photos, 2 Cover plates, 3 Review, 4 Live on the site, each with its button. The plate box is suggested by itself on every outside photo as the listing opens (Box suggested). Press **Cover the plate** and check it; **Suggest the plate** asks again. A photo filed under the wrong shot: **Remove** under it on the Photos card, then take the right one.
4. Drag over a plate to draw a box; drag a box to move it, its corner to resize it.
5. Keep **The CARMA Ontario plate** on a rear plate or **Edit the front plate out** on a front photo (or choose **A CarmaCars plate**, **Pixelation** or **Blur**), then **Save the covered photo**.
6. No plate in the shot? **No plate visible on this photo**.

![](/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-phone-95d5afd2.jpg "phone; size: 390 776; pins: 3 52.6 78.9, 4 50.0 43.8, 5 61.5 62.1, 6 43.1 92.3")

> Watch out: The plate check never holds a car back: a photo whose plate is not checked stays private, and goes public by itself once it is covered or marked. The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately.

## Publish now

Customer service and fleet publish a car themselves; nothing has to be finished first.

1. Open the car from Listings or Field jobs. Its listing says why it is not on the site yet; press **Publish now**. With no rates yet it uses the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults).
2. What is still open (paperwork, details, photos, No VIN yet for a car added by its plate, a possible duplicate) shows as warnings after Publish now and on the car. None of them stops publishing.
3. New cars with their rates usually go on the site by themselves (Publish new cars automatically, on by default). A car taken off the site by staff waits for Publish now.

> Tip: A car not on the fleet insurance policy yet can be requested, offered and paid for, but never handed over until the insurer confirms it. Requests and offers for such a car show a warning.

## Calendar sync with Turo and other platforms

**Cars** > **Calendar sync**: a car listed on Turo or Getaround must never be booked twice.

1. Turo has no calendar link: Turo''s trip emails come in by themselves, find their car by themselves (Turo car number, plate, VIN, year, make, model, trim, colour, what earlier emails taught) and block it with the turnaround. Nothing to set up per car.
2. An email the reader cannot place waits as "Which car is this?": press **Which car is this?** and press the right car (best guesses first). It is remembered for that car''s next emails. If the dates or trip number are missing: **Add as a Turo trip** (choose the car, check the dates) or **Dismiss**. A trip whose email did not come: **Add a Turo trip** on the car.
3. Each Turo trip shows the guest''s name and phone when Turo''s email includes them. Contact a Turo guest only about their trip, never with promotions.
4. Turo cannot read our calendar: under "Block on Turo", block each CarmaCars booking on the car''s Turo calendar, then press **Done on Turo**. Dates that changed or a booking cancelled here show the dates to free on Turo.
5. Getaround, Google Calendar or another platform with a calendar (iCal) link: open **Add a calendar link**, choose the platform, paste it and press **Add the link**. Copy the car''s CarmaCars link for that platform with **Copy** and paste it into the platform''s calendar import.
6. A double booking raises an urgent task for you and an email: move, swap or cancel one trip. A link that stops working raises a task after 3 failed reads: copy it from the platform again.

### Add the photos and readings
A pickup or return recorded with the details later gives Fleet the task **Add the photos and readings for CC-...**. Open the booking and press **Add the check-in (or check-out) photos and readings**: the usual checklist opens without the ready check or the renter''s signature. Take the photos, the odometer, fuel, keys (and cleanliness at a return), sign and save. The task closes by itself; it cannot be closed by hand before.

## Bookings now

**Rentals** > **Bookings** opens on Now for fleet and customer service: the cars out with their renter and due-back countdown, coming back today and tomorrow (overdue first, in red), going out in the next 72 hours with what is ready, the money due in 7 days and the free cars. It refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. A booking listed as **Out (pickup not recorded)** left without a check-in: press **Mark picked up**, then add the photos, km and fuel from the task. A car overdue or due back today has **Returned** (here, on Today and at the top of the booking): give the return time (now, or earlier; the late charges follow it) and the km and fuel if known. The overdue messages stop and the task for the photos is yours. The search above it finds any booking.

### The renter says the car is back

An urgent To do "The renter says the car is back" means the renter pressed **I''ve returned the car** on an overdue booking. Their overdue notices are paused. Open the booking, check the car (place, tracker, the renter''s photos), then press **Confirm** (correct the odometer, fuel or time first if needed; the trip is completed) or **Deny** with the reason (the renter is told and the notices start again).

**Start a listing** takes the VIN from the car: **Scan the barcode** in the door frame or under the windshield, or **Photo of the VIN**.

**Add photos** on a listing takes any number of photos at once, in any order: each is sorted to its shot. A photo that fits no shot goes in with **Extra outside photos** or **Extra inside and detail photos**; drag the extras into their order in the review and press **Save the order**. 10 photos and one outside photo complete the listing. Outside photos are framed big on the studio floor with a shadow under the tyres; a watermark or caption at a photo''s edge is cut off by itself. **Cover the plate** opens with the plate box suggested: check it and save. A car small in the frame, or no model name behind it: press **Frame the outside photos again** (then check the plates again). A bad cut-out (a mirror missing, background left): press **Edit the cut-out**, erase or restore with the brush, move or size the car on the studio, then **Save as a new version**. The version before is kept; if the car did not move, the plate check carries over. Every photo gets a light touch-up by itself; tick **Use original colours** under a photo to make it again without it. Outside photos go in the dark CarmaCars showroom (the logo on the wall, the model''s name behind the car on the cover). A car still on the black studio: press **Apply showroom to this car**; **Listings** > **Apply showroom to every car** does every car. Under a photo, **Redo** makes it again and **Back to the original** puts back the version before. **Marketing photos** on a listing makes copies in other scenes for Marketplace and social posts (choose a scene or **Mix: a different scene on each photo**, then **Make the marketing set**); the website''s photos stay as they are. **First photo** on a listing chooses what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit: **Plain car**, **With a model** (the image model''s car-show photo, a fully clothed adult model beside the car) or **Flyer** (the price a day from the live rates, the call to action and the logo on the cover). Switch any time; until the chosen one is made the plain cover shows.
## One screen, many photos (release 28)

**Import photos from a Google Drive link** on a listing adds the photos of a public Drive folder to the car, sorted and processed like Add photos. **Listings** > **Import photos from Drive** reads a whole folder of folders (one per make, then per car), proposes the car for each folder, and imports once you confirm the table. The page follows the import and ends with what was imported, skipped and failed, and why. The same Drive file is never added twice. Customer service can import into a car whose listing is already started; Fleet and Admin can start one.

Check-in and check-out are one screen on the booking page: the time, km, fuel, many photos at once (tag angles if you like) and a note. The renter''s own photos join the same report; each photo shows who took it. On a car''s page, record **Pickup from owner** and **Return to owner** with photos: the owner sees them.

## Repair costs on a car

On a car''s page, **Kickbacks and repairs** lists its repair costs and the kickbacks partners paid on it. **Add a repair cost**: the date, the shop or another vendor, what was done, the amount and tax, who paid (CarmaCars, the owner or the insurer), the claim and a photo or PDF of the receipt.

## When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)
On the booking page, **What stops the pickup now** (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking''s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: **Ask to record a past trip** with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.

## Incident cards (release 34)
**Cars**, then **Incident cards**, prints the card for the visor or the glovebox: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, our support and roadside numbers, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. On a car''s page, **Incident card** prints that car; on the list, **Print all cars** prints every car, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks. Laminate it and put one in each car. The insurance policy on the card is set by an Admin; until it is, the card tells the renter to ask for the slip. No price is ever printed on it.

## Government forms (release 35)
The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner''s car are on the owner''s page and the car''s page, under **Government forms**. Open a form, press **Change a value**, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and **Save**: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under **Versions** with their downloads. **Back to the records** undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. **Make again** keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. **Owners**, then **Government forms**, opens the forms'' mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under **Earlier mappings**. Only the boxes are filled: the form''s own text and layout never change.

## Odometer and fuel at every check-in and check-out

Every check-in and check-out on one screen asks for two photos besides the others:

1. **Photo of the dashboard**: the odometer and the fuel gauge, from the camera roll or the camera. The site reads it and asks, for example, "Odometer 45,210 km, fuel 3/4: correct?". Press **Yes, correct**, or **No, I will type it** and type the odometer and pick the fuel in eighths.
2. **Selfie in front of the car**: taken now with the camera, never from the camera roll. A selfie without a fresh capture time is noted on the report for you to check; it never stops the check-in.

At the return the site compares with the pickup: km driven, km over the included allowance and the fuel difference. The extra km (the booking''s rate per km) are added to the booking by themselves. The fuel is prepared as a suggested line: the car''s tank x the fuel missing x the local pump price of its grade x 1.25, plus the $20 refuelling fee (an electric car: battery kWh x the charge missing x $0.40, plus the fee). You and Finance confirm it on the deposit review; no card is charged by it. The photo report shows both dashboard photos side by side with the readings and these charges.

## Change the car of a confirmed booking

A car with a problem before pickup? On the booking, press **Change the car**, choose a car free for the dates and say why. The price comes from the new car''s rate sheet; more to pay is left open for the renter, less becomes a refund for approval. The jobs move to the new car and the renter gets one email.

## An accident reported by a renter

A renter can report an accident from the accident card on their booking. It opens the incident with its first-response steps and your To do, and sends you an urgent alert (on duty) and to Admins: what happened, where, the photos and videos, the other party, the police report number, whether anyone is hurt and whether the car can be driven. Call the renter at once; a car that cannot be driven is already out of service with its calendar blocked.
## Payments and calls (release 35)
Fleet takes payments on a booking''s **Money** tab: text or email a pay link, charge the saved card when the renter agreed, hold the deposit, or record cash or an e-Transfer received (within your single limit; Finance gets a To do to check it). Refunds, captures and voids stay with Finance and the Admins.

Calls and texts about pickups, returns, deliveries and cars on rent come to Fleet first: the caller pop-up shows them, and **More fleet** > **Calls and texts** is your inbox. A car late back has **Returning now** on its late panel: press it when the renter says they are on the way, and they get no more overdue reminders for that return time.

The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner''s car are on the owner''s page and the car''s page, under **Government forms**. Open a form, press **Change a value**, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and **Save**: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under **Versions** with their downloads. **Back to the records** undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. **Make again** keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. **Owners**, then **Government forms**, opens the forms'' mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under **Earlier mappings**. Only the boxes are filled: the form''s own text and layout never change. The owner signs each form on screen: the page shows **Owner''s signature** beside the form (who, when, the version) and **Download the print-ready form** has no signature on it. A value changed after signing shows **Changed since signed** and the owner is asked to sign again.

## Close ended trips

A back-dated close sends the renter no email or text. Fleet gets a To do when a trip is still open 2 hours after its return time, and the morning digest lists how many are open.

**Field jobs** > **Close ended trips**: tick the trips that ended and were never closed, mark them returned on time or late (with the time), choose the deposit decision (deduct the balance owed, deduct the late fee, or release in full) and press **Close**. An expired card hold is settled by expiry at once. An Admin presses Release for the rest. On a booking, an expired hold after the return has **Mark settled (released by expiry)**.

## Field applicant calls (release 35)

Field applicants who pass the AI interview book a 10-minute live call in the hour before the weekly townhall. **Field applicant calls** on your home page lists the six slots and who took each one.

## Value and fuel on the car page (release 35)

**Cars** > the car > **Overview** > **Value and fuel**:

- **Canadian Black Book value** (with the date checked) or an **Estimated value (when no Black Book)**: renters on credit card coverage are checked against it. With neither, they go to staff review.
- **Tank (litres)** and **Fuel grade** (regular, premium or diesel; empty uses the class), or **Battery (kWh)** for an electric car. Empty uses the default in Program settings.

Press **Save**. Customer service sees the card; only Fleet and an Admin change it.

## Shifts, delivery and fuel (release 35)

- The shift board shows each field person''s availability, the standing weekly shifts, who is under the minimum, and for each slot the people to ask. A shift nobody claimed 48 hours ahead alerts you.
- You can approve new staff at the fourth onboarding step, or reject with a reason.
- Delivery is priced by distance from 1570 Midland Ave; the fuel line at the return is a suggestion from the tank and the pump price for you to check on the deposit review.
- An Admin can delete a car that has only test bookings; a car with a real booking stays.', 'Fleet', 'Field jobs, daily checks, photo reviews, similar cars and listings.',
  'You keep the cars moving: field jobs, daily checks, photo reviews after returns, and the listings with their duplicate check and plate covering.

Your rail: Queue, Today, Field jobs, Field hours, Daily checks, Photo reviews, Calendar, Listings, Similar cars, Find a renter and Scorecard.

## Schedule field jobs

Every confirmed booking gets its handover (or delivery) and return (or pickup) jobs by itself, at the booking''s times and place, and put on a shift: the shift covering its time, or that day''s (see Shifts and who gets a job). The people on the shift share its jobs, least busy first. You check and change them.

1. Jobs, next three days: each with its place, its shift, its field staff and whether they acknowledged it. "Made from the booking" marks the ones made by themselves; when the booking moves, they move too, unless you changed them.
2. Change a job with **To a shift** (another shift), **Assign** or **Reassign** (a field person on a shift that day when the day has shifts, or an Admin), **Move** (time and place) or **Cancel**.
3. Handovers and returns without a job (when the automatic jobs are off, or one was cancelled) are listed first: press **Schedule**, the place filled in from the booking.
4. An Admin turns the automatic jobs or the assignment off in Settings > Program.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-02-field-jobs-desktop-8e721230.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 565; address: carmacars.ca/va/fleet; pins: 1 17.9 51.3")

## Shifts and who gets a job

Field staff take their shifts from a schedule you publish, ideally a week ahead. A job is given by itself only to a field person who passed the academy and holds a shift that day, and work lands only on days with shifts.

1. On **Field jobs**, **Shifts, next seven days** shows each day and how many people are on a shift, and each shift its jobs (**Jobs on it**). A shift with jobs and nobody on it is marked; within 24 hours of its start you get an alert and a To do, once.
2. Press **Publish shifts**: the first day''s start and end, how many people, and for how many days the same hours repeat. Field staff take them on their phones.
3. **Add a person** puts someone on a shift and **Remove** takes them off. A person who has not passed the academy cannot take shifts or be given a job.
4. A shift nobody claimed keeps its jobs: field staff see them when they look for shifts to claim, and the one who claims it gets them. A shift given up or swapped takes its jobs along; a cancelled shift sends them to another shift.
5. Work due on a day with no shifts moves to the day before when it is known in advance, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day. The job shows its planned day and keeps the booking''s real time; the renter''s times never change. A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning: cover it, or move the booking time.
6. **Unassign** takes a job off its person and its shift; tick **Tell them** only if they should know. The Admins can be given a job too (no shift needed).

